    "narrative": "Our offensive outlook for June 25th leans heavily on high-upside matchups against favorable xERA profiles, led by **Jonathan Aranda** (67.02) and **Bryson Stott** (63.95). **Jonathan Aranda** sits as our premier play today; batting second against an exploitable arm in Lugo provides an ideal floor, and his dynamic platoon advantage (R) effectively mitigates the negative park factor. Similarly, **Bryson Stott** is a high-confidence start; his 63.95 score is buoyed by a strong platoon edge against Cade Cavalli, positioning him as a primary contributor for run production. **Cal Raleigh** also warrants mention as a \"Strong\" play (61.29); despite the neutral park, the boost from his elevated batting order position makes him a reliable engine for our power categories.\n\nOur bench strategy remains conservative as we navigate a slate where several fringe options fall into the \"Marginal\" category. The most difficult decision involved **Masyn Winn**, who sits just outside the 60-point threshold at 56.13. While his elite speed and the \"Slow SP Delivery\" bonus provide a boost to our scarcity-driven focus on stolen bases, facing a top-tier arm like Zac Gallen makes him a riskier start compared to the more favorable platoon environments enjoyed by **Yainer Diaz** and **Geraldo Perdomo**. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** confirmed on the IL, and both **Tyler Freeman** and **Taylor Ward** dealing with off-days, our depth is thin, necessitating a disciplined approach to cap management.\n\nInvestors should monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Yainer Diaz**, **Bryson Stott**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Masyn Winn**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Daulton Varsho**, as any shifts out of the top-six spots could negatively impact their efficiency scores. **Matt Chapman** presents a unique case; while he sits at a respectable 57.26, he faces the toughest matchup of the day against Jeffrey Springs. Given that **Jung Hoo Lee** (47.52) also struggles against the same left-handed arm, we are wary of the platoon disadvantage. We will continue to track bench assets like **Ryan Waldschmidt**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Luis Arraez**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, and **Drew Gilbert** for potential late-game adjustments should the weather or official lineups deteriorate.",
